  • RINGS — wave interference; a 2nd ring system detuned by COHERENCE (aligned/constructive at high
    coherence, turbulent moiré at low) — a literal visual of your signal coherence.
  • CHLADNI — the eigenmodes of a vibrating square plate (cos(mπx)cos(nπy) − cos(nπx)cos(mπy)); sand
    gathers on the nodal lines. The mode numbers m,n come from the SOUNDING TONE, so a higher pitch
    shows a finer figure — a real, physical pitch→pattern mapping. Coherence sharpens the lines.
  • PLASMA — superposed travelling plane waves; coherence raises the contrast (ordered banding vs soft
    wash); drifts slowly via the flash-safe phase.
  Design polish across all looks: a breath-driven central bloom, per-look vignette for depth, and a
  sub-LSB dither that removes banding in the dark gradients. Colour stays the physically-correct
  tone→light (pitch = colour); Hue/Saturation still rotate the palette for VJ use. Flash-safety
  unchanged (every look ≤2.5 Hz < WCAG 3 Hz). Swift + MSL both code-reviewed PASS (struct layouts
