notesR: 10.76.4 confirmed on device — LAUNCHES (crash fixed) and the camera pulse finally LOCKS
  (rate≈13.1 Hz, conf 0.55–0.76). Two follow-ups from the device session:
  (1) rPPG BPM was jumpy (83→118→89 at a steady finger): the autocorrelation is ~0 at fingertip SNR
  so the rate rode the noisy peak-counter. Added a MEDIAN-of-5 smoother + a ratio-gated harmonic guard
  (folds only true 2×/0.5× errors, never a real 0.625–1.6× HR ramp — dsp-reviewed). Steadier number,
  steadier sound, steadier visual.
  (2) "Visuals ruckeln hin und her": ROOT CAUSE — the ring shader animated with sin(d·density −
  time×flashHz), and time grows unbounded, so any change in the HR-derived frequency multiplied the big
  time value → the whole pattern snapped by many cycles at once (the jitter, amplified by the jumpy BPM
  above). Fixed by integrating an ACCUMULATED pulse phase on the CPU (a frequency change now alters the
  rate, never the position) and by EASING every bio/look uniform per frame (HR, colour, breath,
  coherence, density, spread, hue) so updates GLIDE instead of snapping — frame-rate independent, so a
  thermal FPS step no longer shows as a speed change. Also removed an AnyView wrapper around the live
  MetalView cover (it could tear down/recreate the view = stutter). MORE design/physics, as asked: a
  second INTERFERENCE ring system whose detuning is driven by COHERENCE (high coherence = ordered
  constructive beat, low = turbulent moiré — a literal visual of your signal's coherence) plus a
  breath-driven central bloom. Flash-safety unchanged (≤2.5 Hz, < WCAG 3 Hz). Both gates + DSP/code
  review green. INSTALL 10.76.5.
notesQ: 10.76.3 (build 2037) COMPILED + shipped (the build break is fixed) but CRASHED at launch.
  Root cause from the device crash report: NOT a logic bug — a Swift RUNTIME stack overflow
  (EXC_BAD_ACCESS / SIGSEGV in the Stack Guard region). The main-thread backtrace shows the Swift
  type-metadata decoder infinitely recursing — swift_getTypeByMangledNameInContext → decodeMangledType
  ⇄ decodeGenericArgs ⇄ … — while SwiftUI instantiated the ScrollView's VStack content in
  EchoelStudioView.body. The root view's body had grown into ONE enormously deep nested generic type
  (every `some View` panel — soundControls, toolsSection, … — expands its whole sub-tree into the
  parent's type metadata, and 18 chained .sheet/.fullScreenCover modifiers each embed their content
  type). Adding the quick-access HUD branch + .echoelSheetPanel() on 12 sheet contents tipped the
  aggregate type past what the metadata decoder can resolve without overflowing the 1 MB main-thread
  stack. It compiles clean and only fails at launch when the type is realized. Fix: put AnyView
  type-erasure boundaries at the heavy branches (the ScrollView's children, the HUD, and all
  sheet/cover contents) so the decoder hits a concrete, non-generic type instead of recursing into the
  sub-tree — the standard remedy for this exact crash. Negligible cost (page-level containers, not
  tight-loop rows). Carries everything 10.76.3 did (rPPG lock fix, voice core, value-field keypad,
  keep-awake, persistent HUD, visible visual handle, non-modal panels) — now it actually launches.
  INSTALL 10.76.4.
notesP: ROOT CAUSE FOUND — the last build that reached TestFlight was 10.73.0 (CI #2031); EVERY build
  since (the rPPG fix and the 4 builds after it: #2032–#2036) silently FAILED to compile and never
  shipped. The founder saw "10.65.0 (2031)" and rightly asked "kommt da noch was?" — nothing was,
  because the deploy was red. The single cause: the rPPG fix changed CameraAnalyzer.effectiveSampleRate
  from `let` to `var`, and init() then read self.effectiveSampleRate to build the bandpass coefficients
  BEFORE the last stored property (bpc) was initialized — Swift forbids any self access until every
  stored property is set ("'self' used before all stored properties are initialized"). Fixed by reading
  a static default constant in init() instead of self. This one line unblocks all of: the rPPG
  rate/Nyquist lock fix, the voice analyser core, value-field tap-to-type + minus/plus/sign keypad,
  keep-screen-awake, the persistent quick-access HUD, the visible visual-control handle, the non-modal
  draggable tool panels, AND the auto-versioning. Verified: this was the ONLY compile error in the
  whole tree at HEAD (checked the latest failing run's full log). INSTALL the 10.76.3 build.
