notesK: The rate/win telemetry (v10.72.1) pinpointed the rPPG root cause: the camera delivers ~15 fps
  but the analyzer DECIMATED by 2 → 7.5 Hz sample rate, while the Butterworth bandpass was hardcoded
  for 15 Hz. At 7.5 Hz the 4.0 Hz low-pass sits ABOVE the 3.75 Hz Nyquist → tanf() prewarp goes
  negative → invalid filter coefficients. Result seen on device: acf=0.00 the whole session and
  confidence stuck at 0.27, never crossing the 0.35 publish threshold — so the camera pulse NEVER
  reached the bus / drove the instrument. Fix (CameraAnalyzer only; protected Rausch triad untouched,
  dsp-reviewed): (1) process EVERY frame (no decimation) → the full ~15 Hz the camera gives; (2) clamp
  the low-pass cutoff to 0.45·rate so it can never exceed Nyquist (filter is always valid); (3) re-tune
  the bandpass ONCE to the TRUE measured frame rate (restart the window so it refills correctly) — so
  the filter is designed for reality at any fps, not an assumption. On a clean 15 Hz device behaviour is
  unchanged. This should finally let the camera HR lock and drive sound/visual/light.
