notesH: Device log 2026-06-23 showed a CLEAN, stable rPPG session (bpm 61-64, conf 0.85→0.97,
  q→0.99 — the saturation-hold/resilience direction is working) BUT acf=0.00 the entire run: the
  autocorrelation safety-net (PulsePeriodEstimator) returns nil even with a clear pulse, which also
  explains the slowish first lock (~24 s) since the fast autocorrelation fallback never fires. The
  pure estimator is unit-test-verified correct for clean/noisy/random/flat synthetic signals, so the
  field nil is NOT a generic estimator bug — it depends on the real bandpassed window or the true
  frame rate (a rate far from the 15 Hz the bandpass is tuned for detunes both the passband and the
  lag→BPM mapping). Rather than blind-guess a DSP change that could break the WORKING peak-counter,
  this ships targeted telemetry: the breadcrumb now also logs rate=<true sample Hz> and win=<window
  samples> — the two inputs that decide whether dominantBPM can lock — so the next device log
  pinpoints WHY acf reads 0. Logging-only in CameraAnalyzer + CameraRPPGBioPublisher (no signal-path
  change). Bundled with the verified v10.72.0 work (number-pad minus/plus/sign accessory + haptic
  transport pulse).
